<style>
  .panel-root { flex-direction: column; width: 78; padding-top: 2.4; padding-bottom: 2.4; padding-left: 2.8; padding-right: 2.8; background-color: #0b0d12ff; border-color: #4a4b4f; border-width: 0.1; border-radius: 0.5; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 1.3; font-weight: 700; color: #b9b5ab; margin-bottom: 1; }
  .question { font-size: 4.2; font-weight: 700; color: #EEE9DF; margin-bottom: 1.6; }
  .body { font-size: 1.9; color: #b9b5ab; margin-bottom: 1; }
  .task { font-size: 1.9; color: #EEE9DF; margin-bottom: 2.2; }
  .begin { width: 100%; height: 4.6; background-color: #EEE9DF; border-radius: 0.4; justify-content: center; align-items: center; color: #0b0d12; font-size: 2.1; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 0.7; }
  .explore { width: 100%; height: 3.6; background-color: #1c2029; border-radius: 0.4; justify-content: center; align-items: center; color: #EEE9DF; font-size: 1.7; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 0.7; }
  .foot { font-size: 1.6; color: #8f8c85; margin-top: 0.9; }
</style>
<div class="panel-root" id="welcome-root">
  <span class="eyebrow">ENGRAM - THE MEMORY OBSERVATORY</span>
  <span class="question">Can this memory be trusted?</span>
  <span class="body">A recorded decision relied on a memory whose source was later quarantined. The field in front of you is that memory system, as it is right now.</span>
  <span class="task">Your task: find out what happened, trace what depended on it, and see what the evidence actually supports.</span>
  <button class="begin" id="welcome-begin">Begin investigation</button>
  <button class="explore" id="welcome-explore">Explore freely</button>
  <span class="body">Look around by dragging (flat screen) or turning your head (headset). Point and pinch, or click, to pick something up.</span>
  <span class="foot" id="welcome-status">connecting to the memory field...</span>
  <span class="foot">Synthetic field, real engine. Nothing you do here invents evidence, and nothing changes without authorization.</span>
</div>
